<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar inflows at $1.052 bln May 8.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar inflows at $1.052 bln May 8.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-05-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $1.052 billion surplus on May 8 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank data suplied to banks.</p>
<p>Dealers estimated at least $1.1 billion from financial buy was due to the payment for part of a controlling stake in state mining firm CVRD, which was sold at auction Tuesday by the Brazilian government.  The winning consortium paid a total of $3.15 billion for the stake in CVRD.  </p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the Central Bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON MAY 8</p>
<p>Exports: $282 million</p>
<p>Imports: $304 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $1.426 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $352 million</p>
<p>Net surplus: $1.052 billion</p>
<p>MAY DOLLAR FLOWS UP DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $1.193 billion</p>
<p>Imports: $1.218 billion</p>
<p>Financial buy: $2.346 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $1.309 billion</p>
<p>Net surplus: $1.012 billion</p>
<p>Note: Figures rounded off.</p>
<p>((--Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroon, 55 11 2485418))</p>
